{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event is a value conforming to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event"},{"type":"text","text":". A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tracker"},{"type":"text","text":" is a value: tracking an event records it as an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord"},{"type":"text","text":", with its timestamp, the caller’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SourceLocation"},{"type":"text","text":" and its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ServiceContext"},{"type":"text","text":", as one of the tracker’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"records"},{"type":"text","text":". Delivering is a chain of operators over that sequence: Afluent’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch(strategy:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch()"},{"type":"text","text":", the default) gathers the records into batches, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deliver(to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" hands each batch to every destination, as a lazy unit of work. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Destination"},{"type":"text","text":" is a plain sink, narrowed or transformed by its modifiers: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accepting(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" for the consent categories it serves, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"redactingSensitiveValues()"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"droppingCallSite()"},{"type":"text","text":". A tracker given a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Consent"},{"type":"text","text":" delivers an event only once the user grants its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ConsentCategory"},{"type":"text","text":", holding it while undecided and dropping it when denied. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track"},{"type":"text","text":" only queues an event, from any thread; a worker the tracker owns, never on the main actor, does the rest. A tracker given a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentStore"},{"type":"text","text":" writes each record to disk as its worker reaches it and delivers what an earlier run left first. A property whose valid values are narrower than its type is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Refined"},{"type":"text","text":" value, which satisfies its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Refinement"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Constraint"},{"type":"text","text":"s from the moment it is made, or carries constraints declared with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Constrained"},{"type":"text","text":"; the tracker’s worker rejects an event that breaks one before anything else, reporting each as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RejectionReport"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rejectionReports"},{"type":"text","text":". On Apple platforms, SwiftUI views read the tracker from the environment and track what they do with view modifiers, and a screen’s events carry its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenKey"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking"},{"type":"text","text":"). UIKit views and view controllers inherit it as a trait, the same value as SwiftUI’s, set on a window scene ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking"},{"type":"text","text":"), and AppKit views find it up their responder chain ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking"},{"type":"text","text":"); a control’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track"},{"type":"text","text":" tracks an event through the tracker found when its action fires, so each scene or window can have its own. Screen views can track themselves once a window scene or window turns it on with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackScreensAutomatically"},{"type":"text","text":", which tracks "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenViewed"},{"type":"text","text":" as each screen’s view controller appears, without swizzling ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking"},{"type":"text","text":"), and UIKit controls once a window scene turns it on with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackControlsAutomatically"},{"type":"text","text":", which tracks "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ControlActivated"},{"type":"text","text":" as a touch activates each control named by its accessibility identifier ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking"},{"type":"text","text":"). On every platform, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackLifecycle"},{"type":"text","text":" tracks the app’s installs, updates, opens, moves to the background and terminations, and makes the tracker’s records durable as it leaves the foreground ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking"},{"type":"text","text":"). A tracker given the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.sessions"},{"type":"text","text":" enricher stamps every event with its session’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":", a random identifier held in memory only, and starts a new session after a timeout of inactivity, tracking "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionEnded"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionStarted"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions"},{"type":"text","text":"). A tracker given "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sampler"},{"type":"text","text":"s keeps a seeded fraction of the events they apply to, event by event, or whole sessions with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sampler.sessions(rate:)"},{"type":"text","text":", dropping the rest on its worker before they are held, written or delivered, reporting each drop as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SamplingDropReport"},{"type":"text","text":" and stamping each kept record with its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SampleRateKey"},{"type":"text","text":". The standard enrichers, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.application()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"operatingSystem()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"locale()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"network()"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vendorIdentifier()"},{"type":"text","text":", stamp every event with the app, device, operating system, locale, network connection and the platform’s identifier for vendor, each under a typed key, the static ones read once ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" imports every module but "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", a product of its own for apps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that already use GRDB; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", whose "},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" macro derives an event’s conformances"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and schema from its declaration and which alone builds swift-syntax; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exports those schemas as a JSON Schema tracking plan and checks the events against a committed one;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which runs that check from an app’s tests; and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose "},{"code":"withRecordingTracker","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" gives a test’s body a fresh tracker and returns what it tracked. Each module also has its own documentation and can be imported on its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Traffluent","","struct SignedUp: Event {","    var plan: String","}","","let tracker = Tracker()","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: ConsoleDestination())","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))","await tracker.finish()","try await delivery.execute()"]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent"]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests"],"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events","doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking","doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking","doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","doc:\/\/LoggingDestinations\/documentation\/LoggingDestinations","doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","doc:\/\/Checksums\/documentation\/Checksums"],"title":"Modules","anchor":"Modules"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting"],"title":"Testing","anchor":"Testing"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations."}],"metadata":{"externalID":"Traffluent","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"title":"Traffluent","symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection"},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"references":{"doc://Destinations/documentation/Destinations":{"url":"\/documentation\/destinations","title":"Destinations","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","role":"collection","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence","type":"topic","title":"Persistence","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/IdentifyingPeople":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/identifyingpeople","title":"Identifying People","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Traffluent knows people only by a pseudonymous session. An identifier that outlives one is yours to add, store, reset and gate with consent."}],"kind":"article"},"doc://AppKitTracking/documentation/AppKitTracking":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/appkittracking","kind":"symbol","title":"AppKitTracking","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://Trackers/documentation/Trackers":{"url":"\/documentation\/trackers","title":"Trackers","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","role":"collection","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/WhatGoesWhere":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Four signals, four jobs. Decide which one a fact belongs to before you write the line that records it."}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/whatgoeswhere","kind":"article","title":"Logging, Tracing, Metrics and Analytics","type":"topic","role":"article"},"doc://EventMacros/documentation/EventMacros":{"url":"\/documentation\/eventmacros","title":"EventMacros","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","role":"collection","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://GRDBPersistence/documentation/GRDBPersistence":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/grdbpersistence","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"GRDBPersistence","role":"collection"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ChangingEvents":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","title":"Changing an Event","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An event’s version counts the changes that records stored before them can’t be read through, and only those. A compatible change keeps the version; a breaking one raises it."}],"kind":"article"},"doc://Events/documentation/Events":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/events","type":"topic","title":"Events","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://UIKitTracking/documentation/UIKitTracking":{"url":"\/documentation\/uikittracking","title":"UIKitTracking","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","role":"collection","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Checksums/documentation/Checksums":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Checksums\/documentation\/Checksums","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/checksums","type":"topic","title":"Checksums","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://Sessions/documentation/Sessions":{"url":"\/documentation\/sessions","title":"Sessions","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","role":"collection","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://AutomaticControlTracking/documentation/AutomaticControlTracking":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/automaticcontroltracking","type":"topic","title":"AutomaticControlTracking","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://StandardContext/documentation/StandardContext":{"url":"\/documentation\/standardcontext","title":"StandardContext","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","role":"collection","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://AutomaticScreenTracking/documentation/AutomaticScreenTracking":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/automaticscreentracking","type":"topic","title":"AutomaticScreenTracking","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/PrivacyManifests":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/privacymanifests","title":"Privacy Manifests","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What each module can collect, the required-reason APIs it calls, and the privacy manifest it ships, so you can fill in your app’s own manifest and privacy labels."}],"kind":"article"},"doc://LifecycleTracking/documentation/LifecycleTracking":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/lifecycletracking","kind":"symbol","title":"LifecycleTracking","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","title":"Traffluent","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"HTTPDestinations","role":"collection"},"doc://LoggingDestinations/documentation/LoggingDestinations":{"url":"\/documentation\/loggingdestinations","title":"LoggingDestinations","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoggingDestinations\/documentation\/LoggingDestinations","role":"collection","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://TrackerTesting/documentation/TrackerTesting":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/trackertesting","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"TrackerTesting","role":"collection"},"doc://TrackingPlanTesting/documentation/TrackingPlanTesting":{"url":"\/documentation\/trackingplantesting","title":"TrackingPlanTesting","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","role":"collection","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://TracingDestinations/documentation/TracingDestinations":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/tracingdestinations","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"TracingDestinations","role":"collection"},"doc://SwiftUITracking/documentation/SwiftUITracking":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftuitracking","title":"SwiftUITracking","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking","role":"collection","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://TrackingPlans/documentation/TrackingPlans":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/trackingplans","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"TrackingPlans","role":"collection"}}}